our components were placed where they stood in L, the mode RangeBox.SLDASM showed; one no mate holds stands there in every mode. Assembly features, display states and appearances stay behind; pattern instances come over as components of their own. If a part of yours was made in context of RangeBox.SLDASM, it still refers to that assembly's parts. Save RangeBox_r2 in SolidWorks to keep what was carried.
